legend right
  <b>Enumerations</b>
  <b>TrackingMode</b>: SERIALIZED, QUANTITY
  <b>IdentifierType</b>: IMEI, SERIAL
  <b>PurchaseStatus</b>: DRAFT, SUBMITTED, APPROVED, REJECTED, PARTIALLY_RECEIVED, RECEIVED, CANCELLED
  <b>MovementType</b>: OPENING_BALANCE, PURCHASE_RECEIPT, ADJUSTMENT_INCREASE, ADJUSTMENT_DECREASE, TRANSFER_OUT, TRANSFER_IN, SALE
  <b>UnitStatus</b>: IN_STOCK, IN_TRANSIT, RESERVED, SOLD, RETURNED, UNDER_REPAIR, WRITTEN_OFF
  <b>SaleStatus</b>: COMPLETED
  <b>PaymentMethod</b>: CASH, CARD, MOBILE_MONEY, BANK_TRANSFER
  
  <b>Key database rules (enforced by PostgreSQL)</b>
  • sales, sale_items, payments, stock_movements, goods_receipts(+items): append-only (UPDATE/DELETE refused by triggers)
  • sale_items.product_unit_id UNIQUE: a device can be sold only once
  • stock_balances: on_hand >= 0 and reserved <= on_hand (no overselling)
  • stock_movements: value_delta = quantity_delta × unit_cost; serialized rows move ±1
  • sales: total = subtotal − discount + tax; Σ payments = total (deferred trigger at COMMIT)
  • payments: MOBILE_MONEY / BANK_TRANSFER require a reference; tendered >= amount (cash only)
  • tax_settings: exactly one active row; history immutable
  • goods_receipts: receiver ≠ creator/submitter/approver of the purchase order (BR-14)
  • receipt RCT-{BRANCH}-{YYYY}-{NNNNNN}, PO-…, GRN-… numbered via document_sequences
endlegend

